            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41245",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "junrar: Junrar: Arbitrary file write via path traversal when extracting crafted RAR archives."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Junrar is an open source java RAR archive library. Prior to version 7.5.10, a path traversal vulnerability in `LocalFolderExtractor` allows an attacker to write arbitrary files with attacker-controlled content into sibling directories when a crafted RAR archive is extracted. Version 7.5.10 fixes the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41245",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41245\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: com.github.junrar:junrar\nFixed Version: 7.5.10\nLink: [CVE-2026-41245](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41245)\nJunrar is an open source java RAR archive library. Prior to version 7.5.10, a path traversal vulnerability in `LocalFolderExtractor` allows an attacker to write arbitrary files with attacker-controlled content into sibling directories when a crafted RAR archive is extracted. Version 7.5.10 fixes the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41245**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|com.github.junrar:junrar|7.5.10|[CVE-2026-41245](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41245)|\n\nJunrar is an open source java RAR archive library. Prior to version 7.5.10, a path traversal vulnerability in `LocalFolderExtractor` allows an attacker to write arbitrary files with attacker-controlled content into sibling directories when a crafted RAR archive is extracted. Version 7.5.10 fixes the issue."
